Keep the design; fix the stale-accept path (adversary finding, SUMMARY §6 item 2). A trial refusal leaves `accept` in signoff-decision, and the refusal row/wave-end line point to `pdca signoff <id> --iterate-plan`, which records the decision but never deletes signoff-decision (cli.py) — so the re-planned, rebuilt bundle is auto-accepted and published on the next run with no review. Fix: have cli._signoff delete signoff-decision once it records a decision (as flow._apply_decision does), and/or point the row's step at the in-session iterate-plan. Add a test leg: refuse B, `pdca signoff B --iterate-plan`, re-plan, re-run — B must reach AWAITING_SIGNOFF and get a fresh session, not be auto-accepted.
